# Coding Standards

## Structural Rules
- Early return pattern: always. Guard clauses at the top.
- No `else` after `return`. No `else` blocks at all.
- No `switch` statements: use object maps (`Record<string, handler>`).
- Maximum 2 levels of nesting. Extract to a function if deeper.
- Cyclomatic complexity < 10 per function.
- Cognitive complexity < 10 per function.
- Maximum function length: 40 lines (excluding type signatures and JSDoc).
- Single responsibility: each function does ONE thing.

## Type Safety
- No `any`: use `unknown` + type guards.
- No `as` type assertions (except untyped library interfaces, with comment).
- No silent catch blocks: re-throw, log, or return an error.
- Use `as const` objects for finite value sets (NOT TypeScript enums).

## Naming
- Files: kebab-case (`create-document.ts`)
- Types/Interfaces/Classes: PascalCase (`ZapSignDocument`)
- Functions/Variables: camelCase (`listDocuments`)
- Constants: UPPER_SNAKE_CASE (`MAX_RETRY_ATTEMPTS`)
- Const value objects: PascalCase name + keys (`DocumentStatus.Pending`)
- Log events: snake_case, past tense, max 35 chars (`document_created`)

## Comments
- English only. Explain WHY, never WHAT.
- No narration comments.
- JSDoc only on exported functions with `@param`, `@returns`, `@throws`.
